# s4_onnx_file_export (off-path)
#
# basis      peak moved into model conversion (all three param-stream replicates peak between
#            after_model_load and after_model_convert); single pool (host):
#   heap:python3.10+0x13cc27          867.0 MB   0.317 of the peak   <- this step: io.BytesIO
#   heap:libc10.so+0x4a675            605.6 MB   0.221               torch tensors
#   anon:[heap]                       555.3 MB   0.203               allocator arena, never a target
#   heap:libstdc++.so.6.0.30+0xf4979  433.6 MB   0.158               the ONNX protobuf parse
#
# object     in-memory ONNX buffer: 867 MB for a 433 MB payload (io.BytesIO doubling).
#            _from_pytorch_to_bytes (nn/onnx_converter.py:115-132) exports twice, the first only to fill
#            the symbolic registry.
# fix        a real file for torch.onnx.export (write) and _load_onnx_model (seek, onnx_converter.py:212).
#            onnx.load still reads ~433 MB into bytes at parse time (later instant).
# enabler    param_stream_cpu (spills 866494480 B of parameter shares): -19760 kB = -0.74% vs 0.812%
#            spread alone, non-conformant (off-path/s4_param_stream/). Moves the peak out of inference;
#            its share of this delta is bounded by 0.74%. Freed 866 MB verified
#            (spilled_bytes=866494480|params=201), RSS -20 MB (glibc kept the arena pages).
#
# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: python3.10+0x13cc27
OMP_NUM_THREADS=8
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,beaver_reveal_inplace_cpu,param_stream_cpu,onnx_file_export_cpu
